Install AutoKey for Wayland
==========================

From this source tree (works on Fedora, RHEL/Rocky, Debian, Ubuntu; KDE or GNOME)::

    ./install.sh

That puts launchers in ~/.local/bin (autokey, autokey-qt, autokey-gtk),
installs application-menu entries, and configures uinput access. After
that you can start AutoKey from the menu or by running ``autokey``.

    ./install.sh --help
    ./uninstall.sh

Distro packages (Fedora COPR / Debian) are documented at
https://autokey-wayland.readthedocs.io/en/latest/installation.html
